    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Be the first player to empty your hand, or have the lowest pip count if the game becomes blocked. Players earn points from opponents' remaining dominoes; first to 100 points is eliminated; lowest-scoring player among survivors wins.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Opening Round**: The player holding the double-zero (0-0) must play it ('pose' it). 2. **Subsequent Rounds**: The previous winner plays any double or passes. 3. **Cross Formation**: Four bones with blank ends must be played on the four sides of the initial double before other plays extend outward. 4. **Turn Play**: Players clockwise must play a matching domino (or draw if unable). 5. **Extending Dominoes**: Once a double is played on each arm, players can extend those sequences with matching-end dominoes. 6. **Ending**: Round ends when one player empties hand or all players pass consecutively.",
      "Scoring example: Points are awarded based on remaining pips (dots) on dominoes. Lower scores are better. Players accumulate points across multiple rounds. Last player remaining with a score below 100 points wins the entire game. When a player's cumulative score reaches 100+, they are eliminated..",
